course: dictionary
lesson: 13472
title: The hyoid bone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The hyoid is a small bone in the front of your neck, just under your tongue. It is shaped like a U. You may not know the word hyoid, but the words around it give clues: it is a bone, and it sits in the neck, under the tongue.
explain: «The hyoid bone holds up the tongue and helps us swallow and speak.» Holds up and helps tell you the hyoid does a job. Swallow and speak are the things it helps with.
explain: The hyoid is special. It is the only bone in the body that is not joined to another bone. Muscles hold it in place instead.
explain: Always ask: what does this word tell me? Then check your idea by putting it back into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: The hyoid is a small, U-shaped bone in the front of the neck.
fact: «The hyoid bone sits under the tongue.»
fact: The hyoid bone helps us swallow and speak.
fact: The hyoid is the only bone in the body not joined to another bone.
fact: Context clues: the words «bone» and «neck» tell you what kind of thing the hyoid is and where it is.
exercise: «The hyoid bone sits under your tongue.» Where is the hyoid bone? | *In the front of your neck | In your ear | In your knee | On the top of your head
exercise: What is special about the hyoid bone? | *It is the only bone not joined to another bone | It is the only bone that can see | It is made of metal | It is the biggest bone in the body
exercise: «Our hyoid bone helps us swallow.» What job does the hyoid bone do? | It keeps us warm | It makes us taller | *It helps us swallow and speak | It stores food for later
test: «The hyoid bone is shaped like a U.» What shape is the hyoid bone? | *A U | A circle | A star | A square
test: In «The hyoid is a small bone under the tongue», what kind of thing is the hyoid? | A muscle | *A bone | A drink | A tooth
exam: «Tom felt his hyoid bone move when he swallowed.» What does hyoid most likely mean? | *A small bone in the neck | A type of tongue | A kind of food | A part of the ear
